"""
U atom (32e-GRECP), CAS(6,13) quintet (5f3 6d1 7s2).

Pipeline (main = four calls; all functions defined above it):
  stage1_scf  — SCF variants from STAGE1 (strategy mini-language)
  stage2_cas  — declarative STAGE2: CAS pick from the seed row -> CASCI
                pre-flight row -> CASSCF + NOs + configuration histogram
  stage3_scf  — SCF experiments from STAGE3: seeded (CASSCF NOs, earlier
                rows' dm) or cold; not necessarily restarts
  report      — final table (text + results.md)

Strategy mini-language (per variant, stages tried in order until converged):
  'DIIS'  plain SCF; DIIS extrapolation from cycle DIIS_START
  'SOSCF' second-order Newton/CIAH from the current point; as FIRST stage
          it is the tool of choice when the guess is already in the
          trust region (e.g. CASSCF natural orbitals)
  'SMEAR' gaussian fractional occupations (smooth SCF map; regularizes the
          frontier flip-flopping; E/<S^2> of the smeared stage itself are
          ensemble-like, not term-resolved)
  'SMEARFS' as SMEAR with fix_spin=True: spin-separated chemical potentials
            (meaningful for the open shell; UHF/UKS class only — PySCF has
            no ROHF smearing, an ROHF object is recast to RHF)
  'CLEAN' integer restart from the current (possibly fractional) dm

Session-verified PySCF 2.13.1 facts:
  * pyscf.scf.smearing.smearing(mf, sigma=...)  (addons.frac_occ: neither
    sigma nor gap in this version);
  * FCI strings: bit j of the integer = active orbital j; bin() is MSB-first
    -> RIGHTMOST char is orbital 0. CAS column order = sort_mo feed order.
  * mcscf chkfile: data live under the 'mcscf' key (dump_mcscf); the CI
    vector is written ('ci_vector') only when mc.chk_ci = True.
  * smearing an ROHF object recasts it to the RHF class (no ROHF smearing
    in PySCF); therefore SMEAR/SMEARFS/CLEAN rows are never warm-seeded —
    the tiny verify budget cannot re-flag convergence while the mu
    re-optimization reshuffles the near-degenerate fractional frontier.
Enhancement points (postponed): NOON boundary audit (7p); stability tests;
CASSCF multistart; term-resolved (CSF) weight analysis.
"""
